<Project>
  <!--
    C# 15 unions are a preview language feature until GA (expected November 2026).
    Every project under crates/backend_csharp compiles generated bindings that use
    [Union] / IUnion, so preview is required repo-wide rather than per-project.

    Set here rather than in each .csproj so that new projects inherit it and cannot
    silently fall back to the stable language version, which would fail with an
    unhelpful "feature is not available in C# 14" rather than a clear toolchain error.

    Requires a .NET 11 Preview 5+ SDK: UnionAttribute and IUnion ship in the runtime
    from that preview onward. Remove this file once C# 15 is GA and the SDK default
    language version covers unions.

    See docs/csharp-unions.md, Step 2.
  -->
  <!--
    Unused-field warnings are errors, so that a field emitted with no reads cannot land.

    `_hasValue` was emitted by definition.cs and touched nowhere else, producing 19 CS0169 in
    full-scale generated output. The plugin fixtures compile that output on every `cargo test`,
    so the compiler was reporting the defect all along — but `build_and_stage` shells out with
    `-v q` and checks only the exit status, and warnings do not affect exit status. The signal
    existed and was discarded. See `Issues.md` `8f4c1e2a`.

    Both codes, not one: emitted-and-never-read is CS0169, written-but-never-read is CS0414.
    A field moves between them as it is half-wired, so gating only CS0169 would let the
    halfway state through — which is exactly what item 3c would have produced had its writes
    landed without its reads.

    Deliberately scoped rather than `TreatWarningsAsErrors`. The measured profile (19, all
    CS0169, nothing else) came from library-mode output; plugin-mode has never been measured,
    and a blanket setting could fail the twelve fixtures on something unrelated and unseen.
    Widen this once plugin-mode's profile is known.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <LangVersion>preview</LangVersion>
    <WarningsAsErrors>$(WarningsAsErrors);CS0169;CS0414</WarningsAsErrors>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
